# The build context is the repo root, but the Dockerfile needs only app/, tools/bundle, build.sh,
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES, docs/catalog.json (the lab's landing page embeds it) and the wiki's Manual: everything
# else stays out (node_modules, the rest of docs, results). The Manual is named file by file, as in
# features/wiki/wiki.odin: a docs/ line here could let docs/private into an image.
*
!app
!tools/bundle
!build.sh
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
!docs/catalog.json
!README.md
!PHILOSOPHY.md
!CLAUDE.md
!docs/README.md
!docs/BRIEF.md
!docs/USE_CASES.md
!docs/DATA.md
!docs/perf/PARITY.md
!e2e/README.md
!load-tests/README.md

# Inside app/, what prepare re-creates in the image. Do NOT ignore app/vendor/odin-http: the
# vendored HTTP library must be in the build context, and so must app/vendor/htmx/PINS, the digests
# prepare.sh fetches htmx by. prepare.sh re-fetches + compiles SQLite and htmx, and bundles the
# assets, so a local (possibly Windows .lib) SQLite dir, a local DB or a local build/ never ships.
app/bin/
app/build/
app/vendor/htmx/*.js
app/vendor/htmx/ext/
app/vendor/hyperscript/_hyperscript.*
app/vendor/sqlite/
app/data.db*
**/*.exe
**/*.pdb
**/*.log
